# Data conversion between gibibyte and mebibyte

Verifies direct data conversion between gibibyte and mebibyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1GiB to 1024MiB preserves the integer representation across the integer coarser-to-finer scale, while 1.5GiB yields 1536.0MiB; backward, converting 1MiB to 0.0009GiB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MiB yields 0.0014GiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1GiB
print(forward_whole->to(MiB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5GiB
print(forward_fractional->to(MiB))
backward_whole: int = 1MiB
print(backward_whole->to(GiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MiB
print(backward_fractional->to(GiB))

<<< stdout
1024MiB
1536.0MiB
0.0009GiB
0.0014GiB

<<< stderr
